    {
      "id": "socio-roles",
      "type": "Sociogram",
      "label": { "en-US": "Talking about the condition" },
      "interviewScript": "These three questions are the coloured stars of the paper instrument \u2014 the gatherer, disseminator and blocker roles described by Koehly and colleagues. They are configured for family members because the published roles describe communication within families at hereditary risk. Widen the filter only when non-family information brokerage is part of the research question.\n\nThis stage keeps the positions established on the preceding all-contact Sociogram. Do not enable automatic layout here: recomputing only the filtered family subset would make the relatives' coordinates incompatible with the non-family contacts when the completed map combines them again.\n\nThe third question names someone as a barrier to family communication, so frame it gently and without judgement: people usually have reasons, and those reasons are often the most useful thing the participant tells you.",
