      "label": { "en-US": "The completed map" },
      "interviewScript": "This is the payoff of the whole session, and the point at which the CEGRM stops being a questionnaire and becomes an elicitation device. Operate it yourself and use it to prompt the participant.\n\nBegin with everyone and their connections. Then use Forms of support to move through information, practical help, feelings and spiritual connection, followed by Family health communication for the gatherer, disseminator and blocker roles. Ask what the participant notices. Where do the colours cluster? Where are they absent? Absence is as informative as presence \u2014 a person with no one in the feelings overlay, or a family where practical help comes entirely from outside it, is the finding.\n\nMove between overlays at the participant's pace and let them ask to go back. The positions are kept fixed so comparisons remain meaningful. Nothing drawn on this screen is saved, so capture the conversation using your approved study procedure.",
